  <title>Choose when and what to back up</title>
  <desc>The schedule, how long to keep old backups, and which folders to copy or skip.</desc>

  <p>Open <gui style="menu">Main menu</gui> ▸ <gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui> (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>,</key></keyseq>).</p>

  <terms>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Destination</gui></title>
      <p>Where your backups are kept. It reads <gui>Not set up yet</gui> until you finish the assistant.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Schedule</gui></title>
      <p>In <gui>Back up automatically</gui> choose <gui>Every hour</gui>, <gui>Every day</gui>, <gui>Every week</gui> or
      <gui>Custom</gui> (a systemd <code>OnCalendar</code> expression).</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Keep old backups</gui></title>
      <p>Older backups are removed to save space. <gui>Short</gui> keeps every hour for half a day and every day for a week.
      <gui>Standard</gui> adds every week for a month and every month for a year. <gui>Long</gui> keeps every day for two weeks,
      every week for three months and every month for three years.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Folders to back up</gui></title>
      <p>Add folders with <gui style="button">Add folder…</gui> to copy only those. Leave the list empty to back up your whole
      personal folder.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Skip these</gui></title>
      <p>Folders (<gui style="button">Add folder…</gui>) or single files (<gui style="button">Add file…</gui>) that are not backed up.
      The cache, the trash and the backup folder itself are always skipped. You cannot skip everything you back up.</p>
    </item>
  </terms>
</page>
